sentences.text:
This Court has considered the following facts while exercising discretion in favour of the applicant :-
(i) the applicant is in jail since 27.04.2023;
(ii) the investigation is over and the charge-sheet is filed;
(iii) from the record, prima facie this seems to be a dispute arising out of some matrimonial dispute;
(iv) there is no past antecedent in respect of the present applicant as stated by learned advocate Mr. Timbalia;
6. In view of the aforesaid facts, without discussing the evidence in detail, this Court, prima facie, is of the opinion that, this is a fit case to exercise the discretion and enlarge the applicant on regular bail.

Hence, present application is allowed and the applicant is ordered to be released on regular bail in connection with the FIR being Part A C.R.No.11217030210301 of 2021 registered with Sidhpur Police Station, District:- Patan on executing personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten thousand only) with one surety of the like amount to the satisfaction of the learned Trial Court and subject to the conditions that he NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/11033/2023 ORDER DATED: 18/08/2023 undefined shall;
[a] not take undue advantage of liberty or misuse liberty;
[b] not act in a manner injuries to the interest of the prosecution;
[c] surrender passport, if any, to the lower court within a week;

[d] not leave Gujarat without prior permission of the Sessions Judge concerned;
Nirmalkumar Harishbhai Pandya vs State Of Gujarat on 18 August, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/52710761/
2 [e] furnish latest address of residence to the Investigating Officer and also to the Court at the time of execution of the bond and shall not change the residence without prior permission of the trial Court;
[f] mark his presence before the concerned police station in the first week of every month till the trial is over;
7.

